      "precision": {
        "metric": "multiplicative exact-CI half-width",
        "formula": "exp((upperLogCi-lowerLogCi)/2)-1",
        "targetMaximum": 0.03,
        "finiteBoundsRequired": true
      },
      "stopRules": [
        "Never inspect precision except after attempted-launch checkpoints 20, 30, 40, 50, and 60 in a stratum.",
        "At a checkpoint with at least 20 committed pairs, stop that stratum only when the exact 99% paired-log order-statistic interval has finite bounds and multiplicative half-width at most 3%.",
        "After 60 attempted launches, stop the stratum. Label precision-met if the criterion is met; otherwise label cap-inconclusive, including when fewer than 20 pairs committed.",
        "The experiment completes only after both strata terminate; strata are never pooled; failed or blocked planned launches are not retried or substituted."
